New tsx seed/seed-demo-inventory.ts (npm run seed:demo), separate from the
core seed.ts on purpose — that stays the minimal accounts+presets+settings
baseline every teammate runs; this is bulk sample data for local dev/demo
use, populated from the 20 item presets already defined in seed.ts across
all 7 sport categories.

Uses the same raw pg.Client style as seed.ts (db/ is its own package with
no dependency on server/'s Kysely service layer), but replicates the exact
side effects addArticle()/addArticlePair() perform — the article row, its
ENTRY health_check_scan, and (for PAIR types) the article_pair row with the
canonical article_a_id < article_b_id ordering the ck_pair_canonical
constraint requires.

Idempotent: equipment types via ON CONFLICT (sport_category_id, name) DO
NOTHING, articles topped up to each type's target quantity by checking the
current count first — safe to rerun any time.

Entry scores are randomized 82-97 (comfortably above the 70 GOOD threshold
used across all seeded types), so nothing enters DAMAGED. Net/wicket-style
items are deliberately given a low target quantity (2, matching the seeded
low_stock_threshold) so LOW_STOCK status has real data to show, rather than
every type looking uniformly healthy.

Verified against a real local Postgres: ran after a fresh migrate+seed,
confirmed 20 equipment types and 122 articles created (18 pairs correctly
counted as lendable units, not raw article rows — e.g. Badminton Racket
shows 4 available from 8 physical articles), all barcodes valid 12-digit
format, v_equipment_status_badge correctly shows LOW_STOCK on the 5
net/wicket types. Reran immediately after to confirm idempotency — second
run created 0 new types and 0 new articles.
